AC2 — does a GetX-path toast announce under TalkBack, exactly once?
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure. Under TalkBack touch-exploration a single injected tap only moves a11y
focus; it never activates. So: (i) CONTROL = tap a focusable neighbour with
touch-exploration ON, expect >=1 utterance, proving instrument C is live; then
(ii) MEASURE = touch-exploration OFF so the tap ACTIVATES with no focus speech to
confound, poll the semantics tree for toast instances (a contiguous run = one
toast) and count utterances in the same window.
A DOUBLE-tap injected as two `input tap`s is delegated by TouchExplorer as two
real taps => two activations; that run was discarded as an instrumentation
artifact, not reported as a product double-announce. (For the record it produced
2 toasts and 2 utterances — a 1:1 ratio, i.e. still no doubling.)

  BASE, GetX path (item sheet)
    CONTROL: 2 utterance(s)                                  -> INSTRUMENT LIVE
    MEASURE: 1 toast instance, SemanticsNode#406 liveRegion=False
             0 TalkBack utterance(s)
    => visible toast, text in the tree, and NO ANNOUNCEMENT.

  FIX, GetX path (item sheet)
    CONTROL: 2 utterance(s)                                  -> INSTRUMENT LIVE
    MEASURE: 1 toast instance, SemanticsNode#393 liveRegion=True
             1 TalkBack utterance
    => announced, EXACTLY ONCE. label == the message exactly ("equals", never
       "contains"); substring-only matches = 0; isLiveRegion nodes in tree = 1.

VERDICT AC2: MET. Clean A/B on one device, one procedure: 0 -> 1 utterance, with
the only delta being the 11-line wrapper.

